# The ledger of `dns`: what Go's `net` (its DNS lookups) and Go's own message
# reader `golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage` (vendored in Go 1.27's tree, read
# for this ledger of 2026-11-17 by `go doc -all vendor/golang.org/x/net/dns/dnsmessage`)
# let a program do, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. Python's
# and Rust's standard libraries have no DNS client beyond the system's resolver, which
# is `net`'s (`net.lookup`, `net.name_of`). The task named dnspython, Rust's
# hickory-dns and Java's `jdk.naming.dns` as the yardstick: none of the three
# is on this machine (2026-11-17: `import dns` fails, no hickory crate in
# Cargo's registry, no Java runtime), so their `python` and `rust` entries
# below are recalled from their documentation, never listed here, and a
# question rather than a measurement; Java's provider answers records as JNDI
# attributes by type name, which every `lookup` block covers. The wire
# behaviour was observed instead from `dig` 9.10.6 (BIND), the one DNS tool
# on this machine, answering canned messages of a local server.

capability message/value  a DNS message as a value: header, flags, and its four sections
  heroes  dns.Message
  go      dnsmessage.Message, dnsmessage.Header, dnsmessage.Message.GoString, dnsmessage.Header.GoString
  rust    hickory_proto::op::Message, hickory_proto::op::Header, Message::id, Message::message_type, Message::op_code, Message::response_code, Message::queries, Message::answers, Message::name_servers, Message::additionals
  python  dns.message.Message, Message.id, Message.flags, Message.question, Message.answer, Message.authority, Message.additional
  note    One record whose flags are fields, as Go's `Header` holds them; the extended code an OPT record carries is folded into `rcode`, as dnspython's `Message.rcode()` answers it

capability message/decode  a message read from its bytes, names decompressed
  heroes  dns.decode
  go      dnsmessage.Message.Unpack, dnsmessage.Parser, dnsmessage.Parser.Start, dnsmessage.Parser.AllQuestions, dnsmessage.Parser.AllAnswers, dnsmessage.Parser.AllAuthorities, dnsmessage.Parser.AllAdditionals, dnsmessage.Parser.Question, dnsmessage.Parser.Answer, dnsmessage.Parser.Authority, dnsmessage.Parser.Additional, dnsmessage.Parser.AnswerHeader, dnsmessage.Parser.AuthorityHeader, dnsmessage.Parser.AdditionalHeader
  rust    Message::from_vec, Message::from_bytes, BinDecodable::read
  python  dns.message.from_wire
  note    A compression pointer must point before the name part it continues, which makes a loop impossible, as dnspython requires; at most 127 pointers in one name, where Go allows 10

capability message/decode-skip  sections skipped without reading them
  heroes  refused: a message is read whole into a value; a cursor that skips sections is plumbing for a reader that allocates nothing, and every message here fits 65,535 bytes
  go      dnsmessage.Parser.SkipQuestion, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAllQuestions, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAnswer, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAllAnswers, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAuthority, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAllAuthorities, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAdditional, dnsmessage.Parser.SkipAllAdditionals
  rust    -
  python  dns.message.from_wire(question_only=True)
  note    Go's parser is a cursor for a program that reads a message without allocating; here a message is read whole

capability message/encode  a message written to its bytes, names compressed
  heroes  dns.encode
  go      dnsmessage.Message.Pack, dnsmessage.Message.AppendPack, dnsmessage.Builder, dnsmessage.NewBuilder, dnsmessage.Builder.EnableCompression, dnsmessage.Builder.StartQuestions, dnsmessage.Builder.StartAnswers, dnsmessage.Builder.StartAuthorities, dnsmessage.Builder.StartAdditionals, dnsmessage.Builder.Question, dnsmessage.Builder.Finish
  rust    Message::to_vec, BinEncodable::emit, BinEncoder
  python  Message.to_wire
  note    Names compressed where RFC 3597 § 4 allows it, owners, questions and the names of NS, CNAME, SOA, PTR and MX, never those of SRV, NAPTR, SVCB, RRSIG, NSEC or DNAME

capability message/query  a query made for a name and a type
  heroes  dns.new_query
  go      -
  rust    Message::query, Message::add_query, hickory_proto::op::Query, Query::query
  python  dns.message.make_query
  note    Recursion desired and EDNS(0) at 1,232 bytes, the size of DNS Flag Day 2020, as dnspython's `use_edns=0` with its payload

capability message/response  a response begun from the query it answers
  heroes  dns.reply_to
  go      -
  rust    Message::response_from_request
  python  dns.message.make_response

capability message/question  a question: a name, a type, a class
  heroes  dns.Question
  go      dnsmessage.Question, dnsmessage.Question.GoString
  rust    Query, Query::name, Query::query_type, Query::query_class
  python  dns.rrset.RRset as a question, Message.find_rrset

capability message/rcode  the response codes as constants and as text
  heroes  dns.rcode_name, dns.RCODE_NO_ERROR and the other `RCODE_` constants
  go      dnsmessage.RCode, dnsmessage.RCode.String, dnsmessage.RCode.GoString, dnsmessage.RCodeSuccess, dnsmessage.RCodeFormatError, dnsmessage.RCodeServerFailure, dnsmessage.RCodeNameError, dnsmessage.RCodeNotImplemented, dnsmessage.RCodeRefused
  rust    ResponseCode, ResponseCode::to_str
  python  dns.rcode.Rcode, dns.rcode.to_text, dns.rcode.from_text, dns.rcode.NOERROR, dns.rcode.NXDOMAIN, dns.rcode.SERVFAIL
  note    The text is the IANA mnemonic, `NXDOMAIN`, as dig and dnspython write it, and `RCODE23` for a code with none

capability message/opcode  the operation codes
  heroes  dns.OPCODE_QUERY and the other `OPCODE_` constants, dns.Message.opcode
  go      dnsmessage.OpCode, dnsmessage.OpCode.GoString
  rust    OpCode
  python  dns.opcode.Opcode, dns.opcode.QUERY, dns.opcode.NOTIFY, dns.opcode.UPDATE

capability message/edns  EDNS(0): the size of a datagram, the DNSSEC bit, the extended code and the options
  heroes  dns.Edns, dns.EdnsOption, dns.Message.has_edns
  go      dnsmessage.OPTResource, dnsmessage.Option, dnsmessage.Option.GoString, dnsmessage.ResourceHeader.SetEDNS, dnsmessage.ResourceHeader.DNSSECAllowed, dnsmessage.ResourceHeader.ExtendedRCode, dnsmessage.Builder.OPTResource, dnsmessage.Parser.OPTResource, dnsmessage.TypeOPT
  rust    hickory_proto::op::Edns, Edns::max_payload, Edns::dnssec_ok, Edns::options, EdnsOption
  python  Message.use_edns, Message.edns, Message.payload, Message.ednsflags, Message.options, dns.edns.Option, dns.edns.GenericOption
  note    One OPT at most, in the additional section alone, as RFC 6891 § 6.1.1 says; the reserved flag bits are ignored as it asks of a receiver

capability message/edns-option-kinds  an option read by its kind: client subnet, cookie, extended error, NSID, padding
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    ClientSubnet, EdnsCode
  python  dns.edns.ECSOption, dns.edns.EDEOption, dns.edns.CookieOption, dns.edns.NSIDOption
  note    An option is its code and its bytes (`dns.EdnsOption`); the fields of a client subnet, a cookie and an extended error are not read from them yet

capability name/text  a name read from text and written back, escapes and all
  heroes  dns.canonical_name, and every function that takes or answers a name
  go      dnsmessage.Name, dnsmessage.NewName, dnsmessage.MustNewName, dnsmessage.Name.String, dnsmessage.Name.GoString
  rust    hickory_proto::rr::Name, Name::from_ascii, Name::from_str, Name::to_ascii, Display for Name
  python  dns.name.from_text, dns.name.Name.to_text, dns.name.Name
  note    `\.`, `\\` and `\DDD` read and written as dig writes them; a name answered is absolute, with its last dot

capability name/canonical  a name in the form two names are compared by: lower case and absolute
  heroes  dns.canonical_name
  go      -
  rust    Name::to_lowercase, Name::eq_case, Name::cmp_with_f
  python  Name.canonicalize, Name.__eq__
  note    ASCII letters alone are folded, RFC 4343

capability name/labels  the labels of a name
  heroes  dns.labels_of
  go      -
  rust    Name::iter, Name::num_labels
  python  Name.labels, Name.split

capability name/subdomain  whether a name is under another
  heroes  dns.is_subdomain
  go      -
  rust    Name::zone_of
  python  Name.is_subdomain, Name.is_superdomain

capability name/reverse  the name of a reverse lookup and the address it names
  heroes  dns.parse_reverse_name, net.to_reverse_name
  go      -
  rust    Name::from(IpAddr), Name::parse_arpa_name
  python  dns.reversename.from_address, dns.reversename.to_address
  note    The name of an address is `net.to_reverse_name`'s; this package reads one back

capability name/idna  a name of Unicode letters asked as its ASCII form (IDNA)
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    Name::from_utf8, Name::to_utf8
  python  dns.name.from_unicode, Name.to_unicode, dns.name.IDNA_2003, dns.name.IDNA_2008
  note    Punycode (RFC 3492) and UTS #46's mapping are in no package of Rebel yet; a name's bytes beyond ASCII are sent as they are, escaped as `\DDD` in its text

capability type/text  a record type and a class as numbers, constants and text
  heroes  dns.type_name, dns.parse_type, dns.class_name, dns.parse_class, and the `TYPE_` and `CLASS_` constants
  go      dnsmessage.Type, dnsmessage.Type.String, dnsmessage.Type.GoString, dnsmessage.Class, dnsmessage.Class.String, dnsmessage.Class.GoString, dnsmessage.TypeA, dnsmessage.TypeNS, dnsmessage.TypeCNAME, dnsmessage.TypeSOA, dnsmessage.TypePTR, dnsmessage.TypeMX, dnsmessage.TypeTXT, dnsmessage.TypeAAAA, dnsmessage.TypeSRV, dnsmessage.TypeSVCB, dnsmessage.TypeHTTPS, dnsmessage.TypeWKS, dnsmessage.TypeHINFO, dnsmessage.TypeMINFO, dnsmessage.TypeAXFR, dnsmessage.TypeALL, dnsmessage.ClassINET, dnsmessage.ClassCSNET, dnsmessage.ClassCHAOS, dnsmessage.ClassHESIOD, dnsmessage.ClassANY
  rust    RecordType, RecordType::from_str, Display for RecordType, DNSClass
  python  dns.rdatatype.RdataType, dns.rdatatype.to_text, dns.rdatatype.from_text, dns.rdataclass.to_text, dns.rdataclass.from_text
  note    `TYPE65280` and `CLASS4000` for a number with no mnemonic, RFC 3597 § 5, read back too

capability record/value  a resource record: its owner, class, time to live and data
  heroes  dns.Record, dns.Data, dns.type_of
