capability client/update  a dynamic update (RFC 2136) and its signature (TSIG)
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    hickory_client::Client::create, append, delete_rrset, update; TSigner
  python  dns.update.UpdateMessage, dns.tsig, dns.tsigkeyring
  note    An update is a message `dns.encode` writes (`dns.OPCODE_UPDATE`, RFC 2136's zone, prerequisites and updates in `questions`, `answers` and `authorities`) and `dns.exchange` sends, but its signature (TSIG, RFC 8945, an HMAC of `crypto`) is not written

capability dnssec/ask  signatures asked for with the answer (the DO bit)
  heroes  dns.Resolver.dnssec_ok, dns.Edns.dnssec_ok
  go      dnsmessage.ResourceHeader.DNSSECAllowed
  rust    ResolverOpts::validate's request half
  python  Message.want_dnssec, Resolver.use_edns(ednsflags=dns.flags.DO)

capability dnssec/validate  an answer's signatures checked up to a trust anchor
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    hickory's `dnssec` feature, DnssecDnsHandle
  python  dns.dnssec.validate, dns.dnssec.validate_rrsig, dns.dnssec.make_ds
  note    The chain of trust from the root's key, each algorithm's signature checked by `crypto/keypairs`, RFC 4034's canonical order of records and the proofs of absence (NSEC, NSEC3) are not written; this package asks for the signatures and reads them as data

dropped  a form printed for Go's own debugging, an error type or an exception: a failure here is a code and a message (README § A4), and a value is written as text by `dns.format_record`
